README-SRC-LS -- SRC/ls, the source of the ls on this diskCMDS/ls is GNU ls, built from SRC/ls with gcc, linked with os9lib.l forits stat().  It also needs isgraph(), which OS-9's <ctype.h> lacks; ls.creaches it through ISGRAPH() in system.h, and the build supplies itfrom a shim outside SRC/ls.What was changed to make it right on OS-9:  1.  os9stubs.c no longer defines its own stat() and fstat(), which gave      every file one invented mode and a 1969 date.  os9lib's stat()      returns real inodes, sizes and dates, so `ls -i' prints real inode      numbers.  2.  filemode.c's mode_string() reads OS-9's attribute bits (0x01/0x02/      0x04 owner, 0x08/0x10/0x20 public) instead of Unix octal groups,      and includes system.h to get them.  3.  os9lib's stat() sign-extends the attribute byte into st_mode: a      directory (0xbf) arrives as 0xffbf, a plain file (0x1b) as 0x001b.      system.h tests bit 7 alone for a directory, where an S_IFMT of      0x0380 had matched the sign fill and made `ls -l /dd/DOC' print      the directory instead of listing it.  4.  os9lib's stat() never fills st_uid or st_gid.  os9stubs.c's      os9_owner() reads the owner from the file's descriptor after each      stat, so `ls -l' names the real owner; `dir -e' agrees.